 Group's multi-brand hotel platform spanning business, leisure, pilgrimage and emerging destinations.","peer_panel":{"asof":"2026-08-14","industry":"Leisure Services","peers":[{"ebitda_margin":7.1,"fy":"FY26","growth_basis":"YoY","mcap":514,"name":"HLV LIMITED","pat":2.1,"pat_growth":-98.9,"pe":244.8,"rev":200.9,"rev_growth":14.1,"s":"HLVLTD","source":"product","why":"shares banqueting/beverage/business/company"},{"ebitda_margin":32.0,"fy":"FY26","growth_basis":"","mcap":382,"name":"SINCLAIRS HOTELS LIMITED","pat":9.1,"pat_growth":null,"pe":42.0,"rev":59.2,"rev_growth":null,"s":"SINCLAIR","source":"product","why":"shares across/brand/business/company"}],"target":{"ebitda_margin":14.4,"fy":"FY26","growth_basis":"YoY","mcap":543,"name":"SAYAJI HOTELS LTD.","pat":-6.3,"pat_growth":-404.6,"pe":null,"rev":148.8,"rev_growth":-6.8,"s":"SAYAJIHOTL"}},"plants":[{"capacity":"","location":"441, 942/1942, T P No. 66, Near Bhimnath Bridge, Sayajiganj, Vadodara, Gujarat 390020","role":"Registered Office"}],"pre":0,"products":"{\"Hospitality\": [\"Sayaji\", \"Sayaji Resorts & Spa\", \"Effotel\", \"Enrise\", \"Amber\", \"Altara\", \"The Forest Chapter (TFC)\"]}","promises":[],"promises_total":0,"promoters":"","related":"[{\"name\": \"Sayaji Housekeeping Services Limited\", \"relation\": \"subsidiary\", \"note\": \"Listed as a subsidiary in Form AOC-1 Part A (date of acquiring subsidiary 16.03.2016) and in the Ind AS-24 related-party list; described in AOC-1 Part B as a wholly owned subsidiary of Sayaji Hotels Ltd. It holds …","risks":[{"note":"The hospitality industry is highly dependent on economic activity, consumer spending, business travel and tourism demand; economic uncertainties, inflationary pressures and geopolitical developments may impact occupancy levels and revenue growth. Mitigations cited: diversified presence across cities and customer segments, cost optimisation, customer loyalty and asset-light expansion.","risk":"Economic slowdown and demand risk"},{"note":"Increasing adoption of digital technologies, online booking platforms and customer data management systems exposes the business to cyber threats, data breaches and privacy risks. Mitigations: IT security controls and monitoring, periodic strengthening of cybersecurity infrastructure, employee awareness training, data protection and access controls. Also listed independently in the Board's Report risk register.","risk":"Cyber security and data privacy risk"},{"note":"Negative guest experiences, service disruptions or operational lapses may impact brand reputation and customer loyalty. Mitigations: standardised operating procedures across properties, continuous training, monitoring of guest feedback and online reviews. The Board's Report separately flags 'risk of guest and staff behavior'.","risk":"Guest experience and service quality risk"},{"note":"The business is highly dependent on brand image; adverse publicity, inconsistency in service standards or infringement of intellectual property rights may adversely affect brand value. Mitigations: brand governance and quality assurance, consistent brand standards, IP monitoring and protection, active digital/social engagement. The Board's Report also lists 'risk of impact on reputation and fraud'.","risk":"Brand and reputation risk"},{"note":"The hospitality industry faces challenges attracting, developing and retaining skilled talent; employee turnover and talent shortages may impact operational performance and service delivery. The Company reported 611 permanent employees on roll as at 31st March, 2026 across all its hotel units.","risk":"Talent acquisition and retention risk"},{"note":"Identified in the Board's Report risk register ('Risk of inadequate compliance'); the Company operates in a regulated environment and states that statutory, internal and secretarial auditors report risks to the Audit Committee, supported by a Risk Management Policy under Section 134(3)(n) that was unchanged during the year.","risk":"Inadequate compliance risk"},{"note":"Named in the Board's Report list of specifically identified risks for which mitigation plans are being prepared.","risk":"Deterioration of financial health and business interruption"},{"note":"Management flags inflationary pressures, rising manpower costs, higher utility expenses and increasing operating costs as continuing to impact profitability across the sector, alongside the high cost of technology adoption and upgradation.","risk":"Cost inflation squeezing profitability"}],"rpt":{},"rpt_date":"","s":"SAYAJIHOTL","sector":"Consumer Services","sk":{"as_of":"2026-06-17","cagrs":[{"cagr":"~8%","period":"Fiscal 2020-Fiscal 2025","segment":"India cruise market"},{"cagr":"~20-25%","period":"Fiscal 2026-Fiscal 2031","segment":"India cruise market (projected)"}],"drivers":"Rising disposable incomes and increasing trend of experiential travel|Growing domestic cruise adoption and awareness of cruising|Improving port infrastructure and last-mile connectivity|Increase in total number of itineraries and destinations|Very low current penetration (0.01%) providing headroom","industry":"Leisure Services","market_size":[{"metric":"India overnight ocean & coastal cruise market","value":"Rs 8,301 million","year":"Fiscal 2025"},{"metric":"India overnight ocean & coastal cruise market","value":"Rs 5,764 million","year":"Fiscal 2020"},{"metric":"India overnight ocean & coastal cruise market (estimated decline ~12% YoY)","value":"Rs 7,325 million","year":"Fiscal 2026"},{"metric":"India overnight ocean & coastal cruise market (projected)","value":"Rs 18,200-22,500 million","year":"Fiscal 2031"},{"metric":"India cruise market penetration","value":"~0.01% (vs ~5.7% North America)","year":"2025 (Fiscal 2026)"}],"overview":"The overnight ocean and coastal cruise industry in India is a nascent, high-growth segment of cruise tourism. Per the issuer-commissioned CRISIL Report (May 2026), the domestic market was valued at approximately Rs 8,301 million in Fiscal 